cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite the paper below."
title: "conv-vs-ped-tutor: a controlled tutor-agent experiment on conversational vs. pedagogical alignment"
abstract: >-
  Experiment code, pre-registration, frozen result tables, and analysis pipeline for a
  controlled comparison of two tutoring agents that wrap the same frozen base model and
  differ only in policy structure, testing whether that difference couples LLM-judged
  helpfulness to answer-leakage and reduced student independence.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bydeng01/conv-vs-ped-tutor"
keywords:
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - intelligent tutoring systems
  - pedagogical alignment
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
